    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly are delighted to present this exquisite red brick end of terrace Edwardian residence, ideally positioned on Harold’s Cross Road.\r\n\r\nThis generously proportioned four bedroom family home was thoughtfully refurbished and extended by its current owners in the early 2000s, successfully blending elegant period character with contemporary design to create a highly practical and stylish home for modern family living.\r\n\r\nUpon entering you are immediately struck by its impressive proportions and wealth of period features. The accommodation begins with an elegant entrance hall, setting the tone for the rest of the property, and leading through to a gracious bay-windowed living room with interconnecting dining room. Both reception rooms enjoy a strong connection to the central courtyard, creating a wonderful sense of light and flow throughout the ground floor. From here, the home opens out to a striking contemporary extension at the rear, where a superb open-plan kitchen, breakfast and casual living space forms the heart of the home. This exceptional space enjoys seamless access to both the west-facing rear garden and the internal courtyard via French and sliding doors, enhancing natural light and creating a superb indoor-outdoor living experience. A useful understairs utility area completes the ground floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor, a further extension has created a wonderfully private and spacious principal bedroom suite with extensive built-in storage and a stylish ensuite shower room. The remaining accommodation comprises three additional bedrooms—two doubles and a generous single—each well-proportioned and retaining the home’s sense of charm and balance between traditional and contemporary living.\r\n\r\nA wealth of original period features has been beautifully preserved, including ornate ceiling cornices, centre roses, polished timber floorboards, original fireplaces, and panelled doors, all complemented by impressive ceiling heights of up to 3.1m (10 ft), enhancing the sense of space and elegance throughout.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\n322 Harold's Cross Road,  enjoys a prime position in the sought-after village of Harold’s Cross and close to, Rathgar, and Terenure—just two miles from Grafton Street and with a wealth of amenities on the doorstep. The area is renowned for its excellent schools, including Rathgar Junior, The High School, Alexandra College, Terenure College, and St. Mary’s College. Superb transport links include Dublin Bus routes 18, 83, 83A, 16, and 49, with easy access to the M50.\r\n\r\nThis charming home must be viewed to be appreciated."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (1.5m x 5.3m)\r\nA bright and welcoming entrance hall retaining a wealth of original features including polished floorboards, dado rail, decorative coving, and an ornate ceiling rose. The stained-glass hall door and matching side panels flood the space with natural light, enhancing its period charm.\r\n\r\nLiving Room (4.28m x 5.5m (into bay)\r\nAn elegantly proportioned reception room with a large bay window providing abundant natural light. Features include high ceilings, decorative coving, centre rose, polished floorboards, and an open fireplace with timber surround and marble inset. Built in alcove storage. Interconnecting to—\r\n\r\nDining Room (3.8m x 4m)\r\nFeaturing an original marble fireplace featuring a cast-iron and tiled inset. Decorative coving, centre rose, polished floorboards and twin alcove built-in bookcases add character. French doors open onto the inner courtyard, providing excellent natural light and an ideal indoor–outdoor flow.\r\n\r\nInner Hall (2.7m x1.8m)\r\nPractical utility area located under the hall stairs, plumbed for a washing machine.\r\n\r\nKitchen (5.4m x 3.3m)\r\nExceptional open-plan kitchen featuring fitted wall and floor units, tiled countertops, and solid wood flooring. Includes recessed spot lighting and a Leisure seven-ring gas oven. A large picture window overlooks the inner courtyard.\r\n\r\nSitting Area (2m x 4.6m)\r\nA cosy living space with double doors opening onto the courtyard and double doors to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nBreakfast Room (4m x 2.6m)\r\nBright breakfast room with sliding patio doors and French doors providing direct access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nInternal Courtyard (3.7m x 2.3m)\r\nPrivate inner courtyard, providing external connectivity between the formal and informal living rooms.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Return\r\n\r\nShower Room (1.8m 2.3m)\r\nSpacious shower room with an 1800mm shower enclosure, Triton electric shower, WC, WHB, and recessed spot lighting.\r\n\r\nPrincipal Bedroom (5.6m x 2.7m)\r\nGenerous double bedroom with extensive built-in floor-to-ceiling wardrobes and polished timber floorboards.\r\n\r\nEn-suite Shower Room (2.7m x 1.1m)\r\nComprising shower enclosure with power shower, WC, and WHB. Fully tiled.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (4m x 3m)\r\nLarge double bedroom featuring an original cast-iron fireplace, decorative coving, built-in wardrobes, and polished floorboards.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (4.9m x 3.3m)\r\nBright double bedroom retaining polished floorboards, an original cast-iron fireplace, and coving.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 (3.8m x2.5m)\r\nWell-proportioned dual-aspect bedroom with polished floorboards.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nRed brick walled front garden with a cast iron gate leading to the terracotta tiled pathway to the recessed entrance porch with encaustic tiling. The walled rear garden (11.8m x 6.4m) is set mainly in paving with a raised timber deck and benefits from a rear pedestrian access which leads to Kenilworth Park. It enjoys afternoon and evening sun."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Substantial red brick Edwardian residence on Harold’s Cross Road.\r\nThoughtfully refurbished and extended in the early 2000s, blending period charm with contemporary living.\r\nSuperb open-plan rear extension featuring kitchen, breakfast and living space.\r\nSeamless connection between internal courtyard, reception rooms and west-facing rear garden.\r\nElegant reception rooms including bay-windowed living room and interconnecting dining room.\r\nBeautifully preserved period features including ornate cornices, centre roses, fireplaces and panelled doors.\r\nSpacious accommodation with principal suite extension and ceiling heights up to 3.1m (10 ft) throughout.\r\nGas fired central heating.\r\nResidential Disc parking.\r\nPrime location within easy reach of the city centre, Rathgar, Rathmines and Terenure."
      },
